    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ec01f9a4_08486a23",
        "filename": "android/virtualizationservice/aidl/android/system/virtualizationservice/IVirtualMachine.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 61,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944405
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-10T17:53:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t quite understand?\n\nSnapshot will create a new directory with the path provided to it. If the directory or a file already exists with the passed path, snapshot will fail.\n\nWould there be a benefit to passing an FD?",
      "parentUuid": "75655b9e_34684d11",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 61,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 61,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "0a35afb9908411fa2563a0bfe2b0d28a5a376825",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e0699bff_331235e5",
        "filename": "android/virtualizationservice/aidl/android/system/virtualizationservice/IVirtualMachine.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 61,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-10T18:27:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the trouble is that the snapshot files will be owned (at the filesystem level) by virtmgr instead of the calling user. If done this way, then USER_A might call `snapshot(\"/foo\")` and then USER_B could call restore `restore(\"/foo\")` and it wouldn\u0027t run afoul of any permissions checks, which is a bad thing.\n\nThe crosvm snapshot is a whole directory worth of files, so using an FD. Might want to add crosvm support for outputting directly as an archive file. Maybe can snapshot to a tmp dir and then zip the results into the user provide FD as a workaround.",
      "parentUuid": "ec01f9a4_08486a23",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 61,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 61,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "0a35afb9908411fa2563a0bfe2b0d28a5a376825",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a02a707_e4e334a8",
        "filename": "android/virtualizationservice/aidl/android/system/virtualizationservice/IVirtualMachine.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 61,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-10T23:22:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, as Frederick said. Snapshot as an archive sounds good as well. Or this FD could be a dir fd, which is suboptimal because crosvm still has to have the right to create files in it.\n\nI feel fine with handling this case in a follow-up change, if it is going to be big. Up to you.",
      "parentUuid": "e0699bff_331235e5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 61,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 61,
        "endChar": 51
      },
